From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16: Power the
 DMICs from MIC BIAS3

The Vivobook S 16 S3607QA's two internal microphones on VA DMIC0 and
DMIC1 record digital silence. The tree routes them to the WCD938x's MIC
BIAS1, as the Zenbook A14's does, so DAPM turns on that bias when they
are captured. The Zenbook 14 UX3480QA, another ASUS laptop on the
X1P42100 whose DSDT gives its audio codec the same TLMM 191, 204 and 68,
powers them from MIC BIAS3, as Qualcomm's X1 reference designs do.
There, MIC BIAS3 makes both record, and MIC BIAS1, 2 and 4 leave them
silent.

Route VA DMIC0 and DMIC1 to MIC BIAS3.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s16.dtsi
@@ -404,8 +404,8 @@
 				"IN1_HPHL", "HPHL_OUT",
 				"IN2_HPHR", "HPHR_OUT",
 				"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
-				"VA DMIC0", "MIC BIAS1",
-				"VA DMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+				"VA DMIC0", "MIC BIAS3",
+				"VA DMIC1", "MIC BIAS3",
 				"VA DMIC0", "VA MIC BIAS1",
 				"VA DMIC1", "VA MIC BIAS1",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT";
-- 
